name w3-03-weasel-close-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T00:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W3, SORTIE 3 OF 10 - THE SUPPRESSION ELEMENT THAT PRESSES IN.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of BOTH w3-04-weasels-leave.fbm and w3-05-emcon.fbm.
#
# THE ANCHOR: Package Q, 19 January 1991. Six F-4G Wild Weasel covered 56 F-16 against Baghdad, and the
# second of the three things that went wrong is that THE WEASELS LEFT EARLY ON FUEL, leaving the
# strikers without suppression [T4]. This file is the case in which they do not leave; sortie 04 is the
# case in which they do; sortie 05 is the defence's own answer to both.
#
# WHAT W3'S OWN SPEC SAID ABOUT THIS PAIR, AND WHY IT IS NOW WRONG (rule 7 - a blocked mission is
# re-checked against the TREE, not against a gap's status line). The spec wrote missions 4 and 5 as
# `2 F-16 "SEAD" (no HARM - C8)` and gave them the task of making the size of that hole explicit:
# "with no anti-radiation weapon and no emitting SAM, WHAT IS LEFT OF SEAD?". Both blockers closed on
# 2026-07-28. `agm88` is a store row whose seeker IS a warning receiver, `sa3` is a battery that
# radiates, tracks, gates an envelope and fires a doctrinal salvo out of a finite magazine, and
# `set attack_mode arm` is a release cue the pilot can take. There is no hole left to measure; there is
# a suppression element, and this campaign measures what it is WORTH instead.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION, AND ITS DIRECTION: the F-4G does not exist (C7), so the Weasels are F-16s with
# AGM-88 - which is the F-16CJ, an aircraft that flew this mission from 1993. The substitution therefore
# moves the campaign FORWARD in time on the attacker's side and makes the attacker no weaker.
# The F-15C escort of the anchor is absent and is NOT substituted by a catalogue row: `modules/air/`'s
# `f15c` is `ACCEPTED` as a FLIGHT MODEL only, and its promotion gate measures nothing about weapons
# (doc/modules/air/module.md, A13/A15). NO W3 FILE FLIES A CATALOGUE ROW AT ALL, as a combatant or
# otherwise; the campaign file states the three rows it would have wanted and why each is refused.
#
# THE ARENA is w3-01-ew-radar.fbm's, moved 0.2 deg north-west so that the SEAD pair, the strikers and
# the battery all fit inside one 520 s window; every coordinate is [SET]. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no
# terrain masking (C4). Scale: 1 deg of longitude = 93 145 m [DERIVED].
#   `q3sa3` S-125           33.20000 44.20000, `emcon free`, four rounds - the type the anchor confirms
#                           on at least one downed F-16 [T4]
#   the Weasels             spawn 43.98500, i.e. 20.0 km west of the battery, 5 000 m, 480 kt
#   the strikers            spawn 43.60000, i.e. 70.8 km west of their aim point, 5 000 m, 450 kt
#   `q3flk` ZSU-23-4        33.23000 44.35000, on the target, and it CANNOT REACH a 5 000 m ingress
#                           (0-2 500 m). It is here because the anchor's AAA is real and because a
#                           reader must see that this campaign's AAA layer is weaker than the 100 mm
#                           the anchor names
#
# THE TWO ENGAGEMENTS ARE SEPARATED IN TIME (O1's rule, and it is the sharpest constraint on a package):
# the SEAD engagement runs t = 7 .. 60 s at 44.20 E; the strike release is at t = 275 / 291 s at 44.36 E.
# `FBMissionRunner` ends the whole run at the FIRST flight-monitor K.O., and a mission-killed F-16 falls
# from 5 000 m in about 122 s, so an engagement placed inside 122 s of a release point deletes the
# release from the record. Every W3 file with more than one fight in it is laid out on that clock.
#
# WHICH DEFENSIVE LAYER THIS FILE MEASURES: the MISSILE layer. No fighter flies in 03, 04 or 05.
# NIGHT: 03:00 local, sun about -48 deg [DERIVED]; nothing in this tree emits light, so the night costs
# the visual channel and NOTHING ELSE - see w3-01's header for the full statement.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT IS A SUPPRESSION ELEMENT WORTH TO THE STRIKERS BEHIND IT? Measured in
# strikers that reached release, not in sites destroyed.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 90bba24b8bf76fee):
#   the shot          `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE mode=arm class=fire_control kind=surface-fire-control
#                     brgDeg=-0.0572 signal=0.945 fovDeg=40` at t = 6.9 - a BEARING and a CONE, and no
#                     range anywhere on the line, because this seeker has none. ONLY THE LEAD SHOOTS:
#                     `q3wsb`, 3.3 km off its lead's line, never takes the gate at this geometry and
#                     does in sortie 04, which is a formation effect and is reported rather than tuned
#   the arrival       `stores DETONATION ... target=q3sa3 missM=0.00281 tofS=52.08` - 2.8 MILLIMETRES
#                     from 20.0 km. `damage KILL unit=q3sa3` at t = 59.7
#   the battery       2 V-601 away at t = 37.5 / 40.0 from 16.1 / 16.4 km, both orphaned by the kill
#                     20 s later; 0 arrivals
#   the objective     `mission SUPPRESSED ... emittingS=59.7 allowanceS=120` - MET, and met because the
#                     site DIED. Sorties 04 and 05 both lose it, and 05's way of losing it is the
#                     interesting one
#   the strikers      2 of 2 released (t = 275.2 / 290.6), `q3tgt` DESTROYED at `aimErrM` 23.6 m
#   the hard target   `q3hgr` INTACT at `aimErrM` 21.5 m - a Mk 84 at 21.5 m does not kill a
#                     `target_hard`, and at 23.6 m it kills a `target_soft`. The fragility classes are a
#                     model, not decoration
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE ... mode=arm`, `missile SEEKER_ACTIVE ... mode=anti-radiation`,
#                   `stores DETONATION ... target=q3sa3`, then the two `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE mode=ccrp`
#   telemetry_q3wsa_agm88_1.csv  msl_range = -1 for the whole flight: this seeker has no range at all
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the expected verdict, because one of the two `kill unit` objectives
# is on a `target_hard` that survives its miss distance. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE PAIR (strikers that
# reached release, `UNIT_RESULT unit=q3sa3`), read beside w3-04 and w3-05 and beside attribution run A2
# (this file with the Weasel pair deleted), which is the only run in which nobody suppresses anything.

net kari3
  control q3nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member q3nod
  member q3sa3 autonomy free
  member q3flk autonomy free

unit q3wsa
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws3 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.98500 5000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class fire_control
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 33.20000 44.06000 5000 480
  wp 33.20000 43.40000 5000 480
  objective suppress unit q3sa3 emitting 120
  objective survive

unit q3wsb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws3 2
  spawn 33.17000 43.98500 5150 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class fire_control
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 33.17000 44.06000 5150 480
  wp 33.17000 43.40000 5150 480
  objective suppress unit q3sa3 emitting 120
  objective survive

unit q3stra
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st3 1
  spawn 33.23000 43.60000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 33.23000 44.36000 5000 450
  wp 33.23000 43.90000 5000 450
  objective kill unit q3tgt
  objective survive

unit q3strb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st3 2
  spawn 33.26000 43.60000 5150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 33.26000 44.40000 5150 450
  wp 33.26000 43.90000 5150 450
  objective kill unit q3hgr
  objective survive

unit q3nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 33.32000 43.98000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit q3sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 33.20000 44.20000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 4

unit q3flk
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 33.23000 44.35000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 40

unit q3tgt
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 33.23000 44.36000 ground 0.0 0

unit q3hgr
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 33.26000 44.40000 ground 0.0 0
